  "configuration_id": "config_037",
  "reason": "The current best is config_031 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, resnet50, avgpool, weighted) at 0.678 acc. The key evidence: scvi_n200 substantially outperformed pca_n2000 as RNA encoder (0.678 vs 0.639), suggesting a richer RNA latent space shifts the information balance in fusion. With pca_n2000, resnet50 and imagenet_vit_l were nearly tied (0.639 vs 0.635), but that comparison was made with a simpler RNA representation. This experiment (config_037) isolates the image encoder variable by swapping resnet50 → imagenet_vit_l while keeping scvi_n200, multiprofile, avgpool, and weighted fusion fixed. The hypothesis is that a stronger image encoder (ViT-L) can better match the information richness of scvi_n200 and provide complementary morphological features that ResNet50 misses. As the final experiment, this is the highest-probability single-variable exploitation to push past 0.678, since all other untested changes (transformer aggregation, concat fusion) have prior evidence of underperforming their alternatives."
}

